cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CodeTrack in your research, please cite the following."
title: "CodeTrack: Structured Redundancy and Syndrome-Guided Correction for Robust RGB-T Tracking"
abstract: >-
  CodeTrack formulates RGB-T single object tracking from an error-correction perspective, treating
  modality degradation as structured corruption of multimodal target representations. A learnable
  target codebook supplies identity and sparse parity tokens, a reliability-adaptive Tanner graph
  yields a visual syndrome map, and a neural belief-propagation decoder localizes and repairs
  corrupted tokens iteratively.
